<title>PAKISTAN: CRICKET-ZIMBABWE WIN TOSS, ELECT TO BAT V PAKISTAN.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ZIMBABWE WIN TOSS, ELECT TO BAT V PAKISTAN.</headline>
<dateline>QUETTA, Pakistan 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zimbabwe won the toss</p>
<p>and chose to bat in the first of three one-day internationals</p>
<p>against Pakistan in Quetta on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Pakistan gave their youngest player Hasan Raza his first one</p>
<p>one-day international cap.</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Zimbabwe - G. Flower, A. Campbell (captain), D. Houghton, A.</p>
<p>Flower, C. Wishart, G. Whittal, P. Strang, A. Whittal, G.J.</p>
<p>Rennie, J.A. Rennie, G.B. Brent.</p>
<p>Pakistan - Aamer Sohail, Saeed Anwar, Ijaz Ahmed, Salim</p>
<p>Malik, Wasim Akram (captain), Moin Khan, Saqlain Mushtaq, Shahid</p>
<p>Nazir, Azhar Mahmood, Hasan Raza, Shahid Khan Afridi.</p>
<p>Umpires: Khizer Hayat, Shakeel Khan</p>
<p>Replay Umpire: Jackie Hendricks (West Indies).</p>
</text>
